# `ds-app.bbclass`: configure flags live in ds.git (ENG-2126)

Read before adding or changing an `EXTRA_OECMAKE` or `TARGET_CXXFLAGS` line in `recipes-ds-app/`.

- `classes/ds-app.bbclass` does two things: `export DS_SYSROOT = "${RECIPE_SYSROOT}"` and
  `EXTRA_OECMAKE += "-C ${S}/yocto.cmake"`. Every ds.git CMake recipe inherits it: controller,
  ais-publisher, gps-publisher, announcer, cot-xlate, interpreter, mqtt-xlate, planner, sdr,
  processing, and also utils and services. The last two have a `yocto.cmake` that sets nothing
  (`containers/utils/yocto.cmake`, `containers/systemd/yocto.cmake` in ds.git), so their
  configuration is unchanged; they inherit the class because the SDK driver passes `-C` to every
  service and the recipe should match it.
- `containers/<svc>/yocto.cmake` in ds.git is a CMake initial-cache script that reads
  `$ENV{DS_SYSROOT}` for every sysroot-derived path (`YOCTO_INCLUDE_*`, `CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH`, the
  CUDA paths) and the booleans (`SCARTHGAP_HACK`, `EXTERNAL_*`, `SIMULATED_SENSOR`,
  `CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD`). The exported-SDK build (`containers/sdk-build.sh` in ds.git) passes the
  same file with `DS_SYSROOT=$SDKTARGETSYSROOT`, so the recipe and the SDK build cannot drift and
  `DSREV` pins flags and code together. `${STAGING_INCDIR}` is `${RECIPE_SYSROOT}/usr/include`,
  so the paths are identical to the old `-D` lines.
- Still recipe-side: `-DYOCTO_WORKDIR=${WORKDIR}` (ds-utils, cot-xlate, mqtt-xlate: the
  `ds-versioning` side file, which only bitbake can place; the SDK driver passes the same `-D`
  for those three). The warning suppressions that used to be `TARGET_CXXFLAGS:append` in
  controller, planner and processing are gone from the recipes: the ds.git branch carries them
  as `add_compile_options` in each service's CMakeLists, so they describe the code and apply
  under the SDK too.
- A new `-D` in a recipe is the wrong place unless only bitbake can know the value; put it in the
  service's `yocto.cmake`.
- **Pin coupling**: the class needs a `DSREV` at or after the ds.git commit that adds the
  `yocto.cmake` files. The recipe switch landed on the `dexter/eng-2126-sdk-content` branch as
  its last commit, to be merged with that `DSREV` bump; before it, `do_configure` fails with
  "could not load cache" for the missing `-C` file.

## Deferred (not done on the ENG-2126 branch)

- **Dead `DEPENDS` left in place.** `protobuf-c` in 8 recipes and `grpc-go meta-go-toolchain` in
  ds-schemas look unused; nothing was removed. `ds-utils` in announcer, ais-publisher,
  gps-publisher, cot-xlate, mqtt-xlate and planner may still be live: check each service's
  CMakeLists in ds.git for `RadioPlan`, `SystemStats` or `DS_UUID` before removing it. On the
  ds.git branch at 0604e8e0 the grep finds none of the three in those six (announcer adds
  `../utils` as an include path, planner compiles `../utils/RadioPlan.cc` into its own tree);
  controller, sdr, processing and interpreter do link them. Treat that as a lead, not a verdict.
- **The src-pins lint extension is not written.** The plan (step 5) extends
  `scripts/check-src-pins.sh` to fail a `recipes-ds-app` recipe whose `EXTRA_OECMAKE` carries a
  `-D`, and to compare ds.git `containers/CMakeLists.txt` `SCHEMAS_TAG` with `DS_SCHEMAS_REV`.
  It needs an allowlist for `-DYOCTO_WORKDIR` (utils, cot-xlate, mqtt-xlate) until ds.git
  derives the version stamp itself.
- **`nativesdk-go` and `nativesdk-protoc-gen-go`** are deferred: the portal's host-arch steps
  (`go tool swag init`, `go install protoc-gen-go`) use a host Go for now. `nativesdk-go` is a
  `BBCLASSEXTEND` already present in poky's go-target.inc; protoc-gen-go would need one added to
  its recipe (go-vendor under nativesdk unverified). nodejs has no nativesdk variant at all; see
  ds-tegra-distro `.ai/kas.md`, SDK section.
